ons are described in this section, limiting the card&amp;#x27;s closure. The manual alert evidence includes an example unit (v7u_N003237), which may not represent a full requirement." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1120" y="722" width="410" height="110" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="CH47-S02" id="page_0253ab35aa"><mxGraphModel dx="1422" dy="794" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1800" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="v_2239f1e3ad" value="CH47-S02 Transaction monitoring &amp;gt; Transaction monitoring versus payment screening" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=18;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="30" width="1050" height="42" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="v_b9f594a508" value="status=ok | cards=0 | errors=0" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=11;align=center;fontColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="430" y="78" width="680" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="v_6104c2403f" value="&lt;b&gt;SKIPPED&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No section-level executable process, assessment standard, control requirement, or risk-indicator rule found. The section provides a comparative overview of transaction monitoring and payment screening definitions and timing, with only isolated, non-actionable description of screening types and a SAR reporting fragment that does not form a closed judgement unit." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=13;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="360" y="180" width="780" height="130" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="CH47-S03" id="page_722165636f"><mxGraphModel dx="1422" dy="794" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1800" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="v_a572c087d2" value="CH47-S03 Transaction monitoring &amp;gt; Technology solutions for transaction monitoring" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=18;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="30" width="1050" height="42" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="v_be882a3d6c" value="status=ok | cards=0 | errors=0" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=11;align=center;fontColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="430" y="78" width="680" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="v_c663f96bbc" value="&lt;b&gt;SKIPPED&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Section describes technology capabilities and provides general advice for AFC professionals, but lacks a clear executable process, assessment framework, control requirement, or risk-indicator rule with a defined entry point, actions, and output suitable for a judgement card." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=13;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="360" y="180" width="780" height="130" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="CH47-S04" id="page_fb12c4f6e5"><mxGraphModel dx="1422" dy="794" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1800" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="v_bbb9280e67" value="CH47-S04 Transaction monitoring &amp;gt; Transaction monitoring system tuning" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor